From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 22:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] ucm: exec - follow symlinks when looking up executables

find_exec() checks candidates with lstat64() and requires S_ISREG, so
an executable that is a symlink is never found and exec fails with
-ENOEXEC. On systems with multi-call binaries (coreutils single-binary,
busybox) /bin/echo, /bin/rm and /bin/mkdir are all symlinks, which
breaks lib/card-init.conf and any sequence using exec "echo ...":

  exec 'echo Main Verb Config EnableSequence' failed (exit code -8)

Use stat64() so the symlink target is checked instead.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
---
 src/ucm/ucm_exec.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/ucm/ucm_exec.c b/src/ucm/ucm_exec.c
--- a/src/ucm/ucm_exec.c
+++ b/src/ucm/ucm_exec.c
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@
 	struct dirent64 *de;
 	struct stat64 st;
 	if (name[0] == '/') {
-		if (lstat64(name, &st))
+		if (stat64(name, &st))
 			return 0;
 		if (!S_ISREG(st.st_mode) || !(st.st_mode & S_IEXEC))
 			return 0;
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@
 					continue;
 				snprintf(bin, sizeof(bin), "%s/%s", tmp,
 					 de->d_name);
-				if (lstat64(bin, &st))
+				if (stat64(bin, &st))
 					continue;
 				if (!S_ISREG(st.st_mode)
 				    || !(st.st_mode & S_IEXEC))
